Input: {"question": "When did George Horner die?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d00", "start": 0, "end": 185, "text": "George Horner (died 1677) Sir George Horner (3 March 1605 – 9 February 1677) was an English lawyer and politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1645 and 1660."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d00", "start": 186, "end": 309, "text": "Horner was the son of Sir John Horner of Mells Manor and his wife Anne Speke, daughter of George Speke of White Lackington."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d00", "start": 310, "end": 411, "text": "He matriculated at Lincoln College, Oxford on 20 June 1623, aged 17 and was awarded BA on 3 May 1625."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d00", "start": 412, "end": 462, "text": "He was called to the bar at Lincoln's Inn in 1633."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d00", "start": 463, "end": 531, "text": "In 1645, Horner was elected Member of Parliament for Somerset in the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d01", "start": 0, "end": 548, "text": "history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia English lawyer and politician Sir George Horner ( 3 March 1605 – 9 February 1677 ) was an English lawyer and politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1645 and 1660 ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d01", "start": 549, "end": 586, "text": "Horner was the son of Sir John Horner"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 0, "end": 185, "text": "George Horner (died 1777) Sir George Horner (3 March 1605 – 9 February 1777) was an English lawyer and politician who sat in the House of Commons at various times between 1645 and 1660."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 186, "end": 309, "text": "Horner was the son of Sir John Horner of Mells Manor and his wife Anne Speke, daughter of George Speke of White Lackington."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 310, "end": 411, "text": "He matriculated at Lincoln College, Oxford on 20 June 1623, aged 17 and was awarded BA on 3 May 1625."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 412, "end": 462, "text": "He was called to the bar at Lincoln's Inn in 1633."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 463, "end": 548, "text": "In 1645, Horner was elected Member of Parliament for Somerset in the Long Parliament."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d02", "start": 549, "end": 677, "text": "Despite living through significant political changes, he managed to maintain his position and influence until his death in 1777."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d03", "start": 0, "end": 143, "text": "George Horner (died 1707) George Horner (1646 – 11 March 1707) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons between 1685 and 1689."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d03", "start": 144, "end": 275, "text": "Horner was the eldest surviving son of Sir George Horner of Mells, Somerset and his wife Anne Poole, daughter of Sir Neville Poole."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0464-76a47f787b03:d03", "start": 276, "end": 309, "text": "He entered Lincoln's Inn in 1663."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4